build and serve the mdBook documentation site, or an API index of the Rust libraries in scope (non-mutating)

Usage: dx docs [--serve [--port <n>] [--host <addr>] [--open]] [--here] [scope ...] [-- bazel-options ...]

Arguments:
  [TARGETS]...
          Scopes to run on

  [BAZEL_OPTIONS]...
          Args after --

Options:
      --workspace <WORKSPACE>
          Use this workspace dir

  -q, --quiet
          Hide summaries

  -v, --verbose
          Show more logs

      --color <COLOR>
          Set color output
          
          [possible values: auto, always, never]

      --build-slots <auto|n|off>
          Set build slots: auto, a count, or off

      --build-slots-wait <duration>
          Give up waiting for a build slot after this long; 0 fails at once

      --bazel-startup-option <TOKEN>
          Pass one Bazel startup option (repeatable)

  -o, --output <OUTPUT>
          Set output format
          
          [possible values: text, json]

      --here
          Use the current dir tree

      --serve
          Serve docs locally

      --port <PORT>
          Docs serve port (needs --serve)

      --host <HOST>
          Docs serve host (needs --serve)

      --open
          Open docs in a browser (needs --serve)

  -h, --help
          Print help

Examples:
  dx docs
  dx docs --serve --open
Scopes: explicit Bazel labels/patterns (//..., //pkg:target), or workspace-relative files/dirs resolved via Bazel query. Bare scope selects every docs site, shard and API target in the repository (//...). Pass --here for the current directory tree instead (//path/...; //... at the root); --here cannot be combined with explicit scopes and never changes the no-flag default.
Exit codes: 0 success; 2 usage/scope/owner errors; 1 operational failures; Bazel-authoritative failures preserve Bazel's code.
Output: --output text|json; --report has no standard format for this command.
Environment: NO_COLOR=<non-empty> disables color; BUILD_WORKSPACE_DIRECTORY=<dir> sets the workspace start. `dx --help` lists every DX_ default.

